Let F: X ⊆ R'' -> R'' be a differentiable vector field. 
Then the divergence of F, denoted div F or ∇ • F (the latter read "del dot F"), is the scalar field 

		div F = ∇ • F = δF₁/δx₁ + δF₂/δx₂ + ... + δF(sub(n))/δx(sub(n)),

where x₁,...,x(sub(n)) are Cartesian coordinates for R^n and F₁,...,F(sub(n)) are the component functions of F. 
